{"_id":"68d3e715166b018f83df5f63","roadmapSlug":"html","nodeId":"czmIvZYONFDxB2UNpT8U1","description":"# p Tag\n\nThe `<p>` tag in HTML defines a paragraph. Browsers automatically add a single blank line before and after each paragraph, creating a clear separation between blocks of text. It's a block-level element, meaning it occupies the full width available to it and starts on a new line.","resources":[{"type":"video","title":"HTML - Paragraphs | W3Schools","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qis4kAOThLw","_id":"6a71e295b0650226a59f1b3e"}],"createdAt":"2025-09-24T12:41:57.895Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-04T13:01:09.024Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a10b41ba95e0d5c68dede2f","title":"HTML Fundamentals","slug":"html","description":"Enough HTML to read, write, inspect, and understand real web pages.","lessonIds":["6a0da437a95e0d5c68ded033","6a0ef00da95e0d5c68ded162","6a0f1366a95e0d5c68ded2b4","6a0f2262a95e0d5c68ded32a","6a0f33e7a95e0d5c68ded463","6a102d2fa95e0d5c68ded758","6a106a2ba95e0d5c68deda00","6a107b29a95e0d5c68deda53"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d772aea","68b7185fffbff9183d772aeb","6a1485bfac1c5fa9928a2087","6a1485c5ac1c5fa9928a2093","6a1485cbac1c5fa9928a2099","6a1485d1ac1c5fa9928a20a4"],"featuredImage":"","readingTime":58,"lessonCount":8,"quizCount":0,"projectCount":6}],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/html/content/czmIvZYONFDxB2UNpT8U1.md"}